    "result_text": "The change is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe rule: when creating an owner, if **more than 80** owners have already been registered for that day, the response's `bulkSignupWarning` is `true`; otherwise `false`. The value is read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so it's a creation-time snapshot persisted on the owner \u2014 mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` precedent.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`BulkSignupWarningEvaluator`** (new `rest` component, alongside `NamesakeCounter`/`CustomerCodeGenerator`) \u2014 a single-responsibility unit that holds the `BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD = 80` constant and decides `isBulkSignup(ownersAlreadyRegistered)`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 injected the evaluator and reused the day's owner count that was already being fetched for the daily-limit check (no duplicate query), setting `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(...)` from it.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column), getter/setter, and `toString` entry.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions.\n\n5. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column.\n\nThe daily-limit rule and the warning now share the same accumulation path (one `countOwnersByRegistrationDate` call). The acceptance test (`bulkSignupWarning` false on a fresh create, read back via GET) and the full suite pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
